# backup.sh runs on the Mac (bash) - a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise store/checkout it with CRLF line
# endings, breaking its #!/usr/bin/env bash shebang there
# (bash: backup.sh: bad interpreter, or a `$'\r': command not found` on
# every line). Force LF regardless of the committing/checking-out
# platform's autocrlf setting - this was actually observed on this repo's
# own working tree while developing Phase 4 on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
